@startuml
' Level 3 - "I never got the HOMEBREW order, dispute it": code facts, model review, code decides.
' Render: plantuml-new -tpng 04-dispute.puml
'   1-3 Gateway: JWT, interceptor (customer = token subject), Cedar (scope disputes). The tools Lambda
'       tokenizes the statement (Comprehend + 7-digit rule, KMS into the vault), writes CASE# through the
'       case-writer role (case attributes on the role policy; LeadingKeys only on the session policy),
'       then starts the execution (name on the case).
'   4   Build: code facts from the TXN row and Order Insight (C1 delivery = not_shipped: +1).
'   5   Review: gpt-oss scores C1 and C4 from the tokenized case file; ApplyGuardrail scores grounding.
'   6   Decide (pure code, rule 5): all +1 and <= $50.00 -> AUTO_REFUND. Any -1 -> analyst, never a denial.
'   7   Settle: one TransactWriteItems (case -> REFUNDED, balance +, refund row once, REFUNDQ# slot).
'       No free slot -> analyst queue. A replay returns the stored result.
'   8   The agent polls get_dispute: "Refunded 34.00".
hide footbox
skinparam ArrowColor #545B64
skinparam SequenceLifeLineBorderColor #C9CED6
autonumber

participant "Agent" as A
participant "Gateway + tools" as T
participant "Step Functions" as S
participant "Worker" as W
participant "Review (model)" as R
participant "DynamoDB" as D

A -> T : dispute_transaction
T -> D : tokens; Put CASE#
T -> S : StartExecution
S -> W : Build (code facts)
S -> R : Review + grounding
S -> W : Decide (rules)
W -> D : Settle (one transaction)
A -> T : get_dispute -> REFUNDED
@enduml
